{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to f39ed0b5 (census f51f16f4 decisions). Both decided; order unchanged (after the settlement head and the R14 documents head).\n\n1. The Worker operator. The anchor is the deployment's pinned register, read through the one existing accessor artifactsRegisterScope (packages/scope/src/artifacts-wiring.ts:39 at Main 71636079), the same pin that creation admission uses (creation-admission.ts:24, creation-lineage.ts:112). No request-supplied root, membership or key is ever used. Slice G1 of the Git host choice note moves that pin to a host-independent setting; the census follows by calling the same accessor, so nothing in the census changes then.\n\nThe full reference is host-side: the index's own row for the pinned scope id (ScopeIndexRows: scope, inc, kind, genesis) must have kind `register`, and the register object's birth (`nativeBirth`, object.ts:687) must seal that same genesis hash. The operator is the key that signed that register's install: the `actor` of the birth's `founding` signed intent (contract entry.ts:55; register.ts:119-139, Code P13). This is already the record's notion of the operator (signed-reads.ts:5-6: \"the operator key that signed `install` reads the register\"); the census makes it a standing predicate rather than the bootstrap window.\n\nThe predicate: the census is a signed read in the existing `Signed \u003cSignedRead\u003e` form (contract session.ts, signed-reads.ts:12-17), naming read `census`, scope = the pinned register, argument = the cursor, with `notAfter` within intentLifetimeSeconds. The Worker route checks, in this order, each refusal `forbidden` and writing nothing: form and signature of the named key; the named scope equals the pinned register; the index row and birth agree as above; the signing key equals the install signer. Then mode: enforce serves the page, register mode answers `unsupported`, no index `absent`. A membership session, an admin session, an invitation-issued key, a `founders` key and a request-naming-another-register are all refused. No replay bookkeeping: the read writes nothing and the key read rate limit (SERVING_READ_KEY_PER_MINUTE) bounds it. Do not route it through checkSignedRead's chain windows; it is one new predicate beside them, and the witness must include the control that the same key with the bootstrap path still reads only what signed-reads.ts says.\n\nOperator key succession (a later register act) is out of scope; say so in the note.\n\n2. Envelope and bounds. The listing page is `{ rows, next }` where `next` is the last row's scope or `null`; `null` is the explicit end: the index had no row after the last one when that page was read (ask for limit+1 or a second count; either is fine). The CLI pages until `next` is null. No extra page, no inference from a full page.\n\nRow bound: keep 4096. The census bound is INDEX_INVENTORY_BOUNDS.scopes (scope-index-manifest.ts:6), one number; the page count follows (at most 42 pages of 100). A census that would exceed it is `incomplete` with reason `over-bound`. Do not raise to 10,000.\n\nIncomplete: refuse, never report a subset as a manifest. `dap scope-index census --out FILE` writes FILE only on a complete census, and then exactly the existing manifest form (v, service, root, scopes), so readIndexManifest and `versions` stay closed and untouched, including the entry0/hash/pin algorithm and the \"omits its configured root\" check. `root` is the operator's configured repository directory as today; if it is not among the rows the outcome is `root-unregistered` and no file is written. On every run the command prints one JSON line on stdout: `{ v: 1, outcome, rows, pages, startedAt, endedAt, written, cursor?, reason? }` with outcome one of complete, empty, absent, unsupported, forbidden, root-unregistered, over-bound, page-failed (cursor and reason carried). Exit status nonzero unless complete. That line is the persistent outcome record; the file is only ever a complete manifest.\n\nConcurrency: the index is insert-only and ordered by scope; a scope registered during pagination with an id below the cursor is missed. State that in the command's qualification string and in the note, with startedAt and endedAt as the census window. The manifest form carries no extra member for it.\n\nEverything else of f51f16f4 stands: no new pin column, no change to has/register, unregistered legacy objects remain a stated gap, the 6499a12b listing unchanged with its paired control. Add to the witness: a `Signed` census by a member key refused; by the install signer served; under register mode unsupported; a page failure yields no file and the page-failed line; the explicit-end case where the last page is exactly full and `next` is null.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}